  "notes": [
    "Materials: S1 and S2, two ground granulated slags; SFA, a siliceous fly ash; CFA, a calcareous fly ash. Curing 'sealed' is the article's upright columns (sealed for 1, 7, 28 and 90 days); 'water' is its italic columns (demolded after 1 day, then water-cured). A blank cell of the table has no row here.",
    "The article judges electron microscopy one of the most consistent techniques and the precision of every technique at best +/- 5 % (abstract; about +/- 4-5 % on p. 9).",
    "The tables chemical_composition and phase_composition are Table 1 of the accepted manuscript (post-peer-review, pre-copyedit), White Rose Research Online eprint 135530, https://eprints.whiterose.ac.uk/135530/, read on 2026-09-27 from its text layer and checked cell by cell; the number of this table in the published version was not checked. A '-' or blank cell of the table has no row. The S1 column sums to 100.4 against the printed 100.0, and its K2O cell is blank: transcribed as printed. The slags are described as '> 99% amorphous' (p. 3); the fly ashes' amorphous fractions are the Amorphous rows, and the text gives them as 'The reactive amorphous fraction was 0.897 for CFA and 0.658 for SFA', the composition of that reactive part being 'computed by subtracting from the bulk chemical composition the amounts of oxides corresponding to crystalline phases (Table 1)' (manuscript lines 244-247).",
